    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0423" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg389"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 231.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my note of March 10, touching
                    the matter brought to the Department’s attention by yours of the 1st instant, of
                    the Fort Yuma Reservation Indians who have crossed over into Mexico and <pb
                        facs="0424" n="390" xml:id="pg390"/> established themselves on the ranch of
                    Guillermo Andrade, I have the honor to inclose herewith copy of a letter from
                    the Commissioner of Indian Affairs to the Secretary of the Interior, showing the
                    action taken by him to induce the Indians to return to their reservation.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d382-a1.xml" xpointer="d382-a1"/>
